  habitatName: Whale Fall Oasis
  category: Chemosynthetic Succession POI
  zoneIndex: 1
  depthRangeText: "400\u2013850 m"
  habitatDescription: The massive carcass of a great cetacean settled upon the dark
    bathyal seafloor, creating a localized biological bonanza.
  ecologicalSignificance: 'Fuels four distinct ecological succession stages spanning
    up to a century: mobile scavengers, enrichment opportunists, sulfophilic chemosynthesis,
    and reef bones.'
  interestingFact: A single 40-ton whale carcass deposits the equivalent organic
    carbon of 2,000 years of ordinary marine snow to that seabed patch.
